class Solution {
    public String reverseWords(String s) {
        // Step 1: Remove leading and trailing spaces ie s = s.trim();
        // Step 2: Split the string into words using regex
        // "\\s+" means one or more spaces, so multiple spaces are treated as a single separator
        String[] words = s.trim().split("\\s+");
        
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        // Step 3: Traverse the words array in reverse order
        for(int i=words.length-1; i>=0; i--){
            sb.append(words[i]);
            // If it's not the last word, add a space after it
            if(i>0) sb.append(" ");
        }
        return sb.toString();
    }
}

Time Complexity: O(n) (where n = length of the string).
Space Complexity: O(n) (for storing words and result).
